Apple swift-corelibs-libdispatch
================================

url    = https://github.com/apple/swift-corelibs-libdispatch.git
tag    = none: pinned to the revision listed by Gershwin Developer corelibs (2026-07-26 pins)
commit = 95f592ab637c4d7916fa05d4d80cbc1ec7d0b2b8
date   = 2026-07-08

This revision is built by tools/desktop/build-gnustep.sh, which
foxyn-desktop(8) runs on the desktop image (tools/linux/build.sh desktop):
it downloads the revision's archive and checks its SHA-256, applies
tools/desktop/patches/libdispatch-dragonfly.txt and installs in /System
with GNUstep (docs/desktop-libdispatch.md). It is
not part of buildworld. Keep build output outside the submodule. When
upgrading, update the revision and checksum in build-gnustep.sh too.

License: Apache-2.0; see LICENSE and per-file notices. These are source-tree notices, not a
completed file-level distribution audit. Check third-party code and assets,
preserve applicable notices and satisfy source obligations before shipping.

When upgrading, review GNUstep ABI, build order, compatible Gershwin
revisions, portability changes and license notices; run the desktop build
and runtime tests against the complete selected set.
